# Binaries
# The leading slash is REQUIRED. Without it this pattern also matches the
# cmd/keel directory, and the only entrypoint this project has disappears from
# the repository with no warning.
/bin/
/keel

# Env
.env
.env.*

# Claude Code personal settings
.claude/settings.local.json

# One-off spike output
/scripts/spike/out/

# Stray copies of evidence files at the repository root. One of these was
# committed by accident on 21 August 2026: a 349 line truncated copy of
# docs/evidences/spike_result_2.txt, still carrying the pre-translation header.
# The evidence lives in docs/evidences/ and nowhere else.
/spike_result*.txt
/spike_results*.txt

# OS
.DS_Store

# Cross-validation recordings. `keel record` writes one gzipped file per pair per
# ledger here, and two weeks of eight assets every thirty minutes is thousands of
# files. The SOW asks for the comparison RESULTS, which go into
# docs/methodology/10-validation.md, not for the whole archive, so the raw stream
# stays out of git. scripts/audit-verification.sh and arch_test.go already skip
# this directory, which is why it needs no row in the CLAUDE.md zone map.
#
# recordings/samples/ is the exception and it is deliberate: the header of
# migrations/0001_core.sql promises that 60 recordings go into git as evidence.
# The pattern has to be `/recordings/*` rather than `/recordings/` for the
# negation below to work at all, because git cannot re-include a path inside a
# directory it has already excluded.
#
# THE NAME IS PLURAL, and it was singular here until 25 August 2026. docs/
# methodology/10-validation.md line 112 names `recordings/samples/` as where the
# cross-validation evidence lives, and this file re-included `recordings/sample/`,
# so evidence placed where the methodology says to put it was silently ignored by
# git. The methodology won the tie because it is the paid deliverable and this is
# plumbing; the README was moved to match at the same time.
/recordings/*
!/recordings/samples/

# Measurement output. `keel divergence` writes one raw Horizon response per pair
# plus a CSV and a summary here, and a sixty-pair run is sixty JSON bodies.
#
# The RESULT of a measurement is its summary counts, which go into a commit
# message or a decision record where they can be argued with. The raw responses
# are the evidence for one run against a market that has already moved by the time
# anybody reads them, so they stay out of git for the same reason recordings/ does.
# A reading that has to be permanent belongs in docs/evidences/ with a ledger
# sequence attached, which is what that directory's zone row requires of it.
/measurements/

# Context files
/docs/context/*

# Internal working documents. DEC-004 section 2 requires these OUT before the
# repository is public: the pre-development memo, the execution plan, the audit,
# the handoff and the deliverable breakdown carry criticism of the repository,
# corrections to the SOW, and an allocation of working hours.
#
# UNTRACKED ON 25 AUGUST 2026, AFTER the repository was already public, which is
# the wrong order and is written down here rather than tidied away. The files stay
# on disk because the audit script and the journal command still read them locally.
#
# THIS DOES NOT UNDO THE EXPOSURE. DEC-004 says so in as many words: git rm alone
# is not sufficient, because every one of these files stays readable at any earlier
# commit to anyone who clones. Closing that needs a history rewrite or a fresh
# repository, and that decision is Al's.
/docs/internal/

# The prepared clean-history migration, kept LOCAL and deliberately untracked.
#
# scripts/history-migration/ holds RUNBOOK.md and verify-clean.sh, prepared on 25
# August 2026 and not executed. verify-clean.sh is a scanner, so it carries every
# marker it hunts for as literal text, and the runbook quotes the same markers
# while explaining the exposure: the personal email present in all 59 commits as
# author and committer, the counterparty named in the SoW, the budget figure, and
# the internal document names.
#
# Committing them would publish exactly the strings the runbook exists to remove,
# in a repository that has been public since 2026-08-18T15:47:52Z, and would add
# them to the history that same runbook plans to rewrite. So they stay on disk and
# out of git. scripts/audit-verification.sh skips the directory, the same way it
# skips recordings/ and for the same reason, which is why it needs no row in the
# CLAUDE.md zone map.
/scripts/history-migration/

# The red zone work report, written for Al on 26 August 2026 and kept LOCAL.
#
# Same category as /docs/internal/ above: it carries an allocation of work and
# criticism of the repository, which is exactly what DEC-004 section 2 took out
# before this repository went public. It is also written in Indonesian, and
# DEC-005 makes English the repository language, so committing it would break two
# rules at once. If it is ever wanted in git it has to be translated first and
# rethought second.
/laporan_pekerjaan_al.md
